<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 18 January, from 1126 to 1958.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1126">1126 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">900 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Huizong abdicates in favour of his son Qinzong</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With Jin troops across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> and in sight of the capital, Bianjing, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-huizong">Emperor Huizong</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> abdicated in favour of his eldest son, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-qinzong">Zhao Huan</a>. As Emperor Qinzong he was the last ruler of the Northern Song.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-qinzong">Emperor Qinzong</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1535">1535 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">491 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Francisco Pizarro founds Lima</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pizarro founded the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">City of Kings</a>' on the Rímac river near the Pacific coast. Lima became the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-peru">Viceroyalty of Peru</a>, created in 1542, and the centre of Spanish rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-peru">Viceroyalty of Peru</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1654">1654 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">372 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pereiaslav Council places the Cossack Hetmanate under the Tsar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hetman">Hetman</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohdan-khmelnytsky">Bohdan Khmelnytsky</a> and his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> officers swore allegiance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexis-of-russia">Tsar Alexei</a> in return for protection against Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>. The agreement's meaning remains disputed in Ukrainian and Russian history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/tsardom-of-russia">Tsardom of Russia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohdan-khmelnytsky">Bohdan Khmelnytsky</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hetman">Hetman</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1778">1778 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">248 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James Cook becomes the first European to sight Hawaii</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On his third voyage, Cook sighted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oahu">Oahu</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kauai">Kauai</a>, where he landed two days later. He named the archipelago the Sandwich Islands and was killed there in February 1779.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1871">1871 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">155 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wilhelm I proclaimed German Emperor at Versailles</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hall-of-mirrors">Hall of Mirrors</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> still under siege, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>'s king was proclaimed Emperor of a united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Bismarck's creation dominated continental <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> until 1918.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hall-of-mirrors">Hall of Mirrors</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-i">Wilhelm I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1915">1915 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">111 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Japan presents its Twenty-One Demands to China</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> secretly pressed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-shikai">Yuan Shikai</a>'s government for extensive rights in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> and beyond. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> accepted a reduced version under ultimatum, fuelling Chinese nationalism against Japan.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1943">1943 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">83 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet forces open a land corridor into besieged Leningrad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Operation Iskra, Soviet troops linked up south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ladoga">Lake Ladoga</a>, creating a narrow corridor into Leningrad after 16 months of siege. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a> was finally lifted in January 1944.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1958">1958 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">68 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Willie O'Ree breaks the NHL colour barrier</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Playing for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> Bruins against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a> Canadiens, Willie O'Ree became the first Black player in the National Hockey League, despite being almost blind in one eye.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 18 January <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/isabella-jagiellon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/isabella-jagiellon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Isabella Jagiellon</span><span class="tp">1519–1559</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pratap-singh-of-satara"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pratap-singh-of-satara.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pratap Singh of Satara</span><span class="tp">1793–1847</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edmund-barton"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edmund-barton.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edmund Barton</span><span class="tp">1849–1920</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ruben-dario"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ruben-dario.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rubén Darío</span><span class="tp">1867–1916</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henri-giraud"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henri-giraud.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henri Giraud</span><span class="tp">1879–1949</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jose-maria-arguedas"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jose-maria-arguedas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">José María Arguedas</span><span class="tp">1911–1969</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/paul-keating"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/paul-keating.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Paul Keating</span><span class="tp">b. 1944</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 18 January <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/odilo-of-bavaria"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Odilo of Bavaria</span><span class="tp">d. 748</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/khumarawayh"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/khumarawayh.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Khumarawayh</span><span class="tp">864–896</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tamar-of-georgia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tamar-of-georgia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tamar of Georgia</span><span class="tp">c. 1160–1213</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jobst-of-moravia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jobst-of-moravia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jobst of Moravia</span><span class="tp">1351–1411</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-duke-of-bavaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-ix-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis IX, Duke of Bavaria</span><span class="tp">1417–1479</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/margaret-of-parma"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/margaret-of-parma.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Margaret of Parma</span><span class="tp">1522–1586</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jan-van-riebeeck"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jan-van-riebeeck.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jan van Riebeeck</span><span class="tp">1619–1677</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-pats"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/konstantin-pats.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Konstantin Päts</span><span class="tp">1874–1956</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
